        ["Who sailed to America in 1492?","Christopher Columbus",["Marco Polo","James Cook","Vasco da Gama"],"He thought he was in the Indies.","Columbus crossed the Atlantic Ocean in 1492.","He called the inhabitants \"Indians\" because he thought he was in the Indies."],
        ["Whose expedition was the first to sail around the world?","Ferdinand Magellan",["Columbus","Abel Tasman","Willem Barentsz"],"He did not live to see the end himself.","Magellan's fleet was the first to sail all the way around the world.","Of the 270 crew members only 18 came back."],
        ["Which Dutchman spent a winter on Nova Zembla?","Willem Barentsz",["Abel Tasman","Piet Hein","Michiel de Ruyter"],"He was looking for a northern route to Asia.","Barentsz and his men were stuck for a winter in 1596 in the Safe House.","The Barents Sea is named after him."],
        ["Who is Tasmania named after?","Abel Tasman",["Marco Polo","James Cook","Willem Barentsz"],"A Dutch seafarer.","Abel Tasman discovered the island now called Tasmania in 1642.","He was also the first European to see New Zealand."],
        ["Which Venetian travelled to China in the Middle Ages?","Marco Polo",["Columbus","Magellan","Cook"],"He wrote a famous travel book.","Marco Polo travelled along the Silk Road to the court of Kublai Khan.","His book made Europeans curious about Asia."],
        ["Who reached the South Pole first, in 1911?","Roald Amundsen",["Robert Scott","Ernest Shackleton","Edmund Hillary"],"A Norwegian with sled dogs.","Amundsen reached the South Pole on 14 December 1911.","His rival Scott arrived five weeks later."],
        ["Who stood on top of Mount Everest first, in 1953?","Edmund Hillary and Tenzing Norgay",["Amundsen and Scott","Columbus and Magellan","Armstrong and Aldrin"],"A New Zealander and a Sherpa.","Hillary and Norgay reached the summit of Everest in 1953.","Everest is 8,849 metres high."],
        ["Which instrument did sailors use to measure their position by the stars?","A sextant",["Binoculars","A barometer","A stopwatch"],"You measure the angle between a star and the horizon.","With a sextant you measure how high a star or the sun stands.","From that you could work out your latitude."],
        ["Which disease did sailors get from a lack of vitamin C?","Scurvy",["The plague","Flu","Malaria"],"Lemons helped against it.","Scurvy is caused by a shortage of vitamin C.","British sailors were given lime juice and were therefore called \"limeys\"."],
        ["Which sea route to India did Vasco da Gama find?","Around Africa",["Over the North Pole","Through the Panama Canal","Over land"],"Past the Cape of Good Hope.","Vasco da Gama sailed around Africa to India in 1498.","Spices no longer had to come over land."]
