        ["Why does an egg float in salt water but sink in plain water?","Salt water is heavier",["The egg gets lighter","Salt makes holes","The egg gets bigger"],"It is about density.","Salt makes water denser, so the egg is pushed up.","In the Dead Sea you float by yourself because of the salt."],
        ["What does the candle-under-a-glass experiment prove?","Fire needs oxygen",["Fire needs water","Glass burns","Candles go out by themselves"],"The flame goes out when the air is used up.","Under the glass the oxygen runs out and the candle goes out.","That is why you can smother a flame with a lid."],
        ["How do you make a rainbow with a glass of water?","Let sunlight bend through the water",["Stir very fast","Add salt","Heat the water"],"Water works like a prism.","Water splits white light into all the colours of the rainbow.","A real rainbow is made by millions of raindrops."],
        ["Why does a balloon stick to the wall after you rub it on your hair?","Static electricity",["Glue","Heat","Air"],"Tiny particles move.","Rubbing charges the balloon with electricity that attracts the wall.","Lightning is the same kind of electricity, only enormous."],
        ['Why is it better to run an experiment more than once?','To rule out coincidence',['To finish faster','To use more supplies','To test the goggles'],'Once could just be luck.','Doing a test again makes sure the result was no coincidence.','That is why scientists write down how many times they measured.'],
        ["Why does ice melt faster when you sprinkle salt on it?","Salt lowers the melting point",["Salt is warm","Salt is heavy","Salt attracts sun"],"That is why we grit the roads.","Salt makes water freeze only at a lower temperature.","Gritting lorries use salt against ice."],
        ["What happens to the volume of water when it freezes?","It gets bigger",["It gets smaller","It stays the same","It disappears"],"That is why bottles burst in the freezer.","Frozen water takes up more space than liquid water.","That is why ice floats on water."],
        ["Why do you see lightning before you hear thunder?","Light is faster than sound",["Sound is faster","Thunder comes from far away","Your eyes are faster"],"Count the seconds to estimate the distance.","Light arrives almost instantly; sound takes three seconds per kilometre.","Every three seconds between flash and bang is about one kilometre."],
        ["What do you make with a magnetised needle floating on water?","A homemade compass",["A thermometer","A scale","A lamp"],"The needle turns north.","A magnetised needle on water turns to the north.","That is how the very first compasses worked."]
