        ["Which invention by Willem Einthoven measures your heartbeat?","The electrocardiograph",["The X-ray","The stethoscope","The thermometer"],"A Dutchman won the Nobel Prize for it.","Einthoven invented the machine that draws the electricity of your heart: the ECG.","His first machine weighed 270 kilos."],
        ["Who is seen as the first computer programmer?","Ada Lovelace",["Bill Gates","Alan Turing","Steve Jobs"],"A woman from the 19th century.","Ada Lovelace wrote the first program for a calculating machine in 1843.","A programming language is named after her: Ada."],
        ["Which Dutchman made the first microscope that could show bacteria?","Antoni van Leeuwenhoek",["Christiaan Huygens","Willem Einthoven","Hendrik Lorentz"],"A cloth merchant from Delft.","Van Leeuwenhoek was the first to see bacteria through his homemade lenses.","He called them \"little animals\"."],
        ["Who invented the World Wide Web?","Tim Berners-Lee",["Mark Zuckerberg","Elon Musk","Steve Jobs"],"He worked at CERN.","Tim Berners-Lee invented the World Wide Web in 1989.","He gave his invention to the world for free."],
        ["Which Dutchman invented the pendulum clock?","Christiaan Huygens",["Antoni van Leeuwenhoek","Simon Stevin","Cornelis Drebbel"],"He also discovered the moon Titan.","Huygens built the first accurate pendulum clock in 1656.","His clock was off by only ten seconds a day."],
        ["What did the Wright brothers invent?","The first powered aeroplane",["The car","The steam train","The helicopter"],"Their first flight lasted 12 seconds.","The Wright brothers were the first to fly a powered aeroplane in 1903.","The first flight was shorter than the wingspan of a Boeing 747."]
